---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import { readReader } from '../lib/reader/cookies';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
const reader = readReader(Astro.cookies, Astro.url.protocol === 'https:');
---
<BaseLayout title={`About · ${SITE.name}`} description={SITE.description} reader={reader}>
  <article class="page prose-page" style="padding-bottom:48px">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>{SITE.tagline}</h1>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>{SITE.description}</p>
      <p>This is the place you open when you want the new stuff: stars, sites, VR, games, AI, and the toys that go with them. One desk, one search, instead of twelve tabs. It is written for people who watch, not for people who run a studio.</p>
      <p>This folder is the phase 1 shell: a server-rendered front end aimed at Cloudflare, with example stories in local MDX. The previous app stays where it is. Supabase, Amazon SES, and the agent publishing desk are later seams, not features of this build.</p>
      <h2 id="seed">The example desk</h2>
      <p>Every story, score, price, star, and site on this shell is seed content. Names like Nova Lane are made up. Scores are example lab cards so the components exist. They are not published tests. Prices are not offers.</p>
      <p>Sister sites stay in the footer: <a href="https://companionhub.app">companionhub.app</a>. The DeviantArt studio URL is still the owner's to add.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
